  "digest_cases": {
    "frame": "Byte offset + y * row_stride_bytes + x * channels + c holds (7*x + 13*y + 61*c) % 256 for channel c (R, G, B, then A) of pixel (x, y); every other byte, the plane offset and the end of each padded row, holds 171.",
    "tensor": "expected_sha256 is the SHA-256 of the preprocessed NCHW float32 tensor as little-endian bytes: each value is pixel / 255 as a float32 division (a float64 division rounded to float32 gives the same bits; multiplying by 1/255 differs in 126 of the 256 values), the letterbox fill 114 / 255 the same way. samples hold channel, y, x and the value there, to show where two tensors part.",
    "cases": [
